.TH str_case_diff 3
.SH NAME
str_case_diff \- compare two strings case-insensitively
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <str.h>

int str_case_diff(const void* \fIp1\fP, const void* \fIp2\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
str_case_diff compares the null-terminated strings \fIp1\fP and \fIp2\fP
without regard to case.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 if the strings are equal, or the difference between the first
non-matching characters (converted to lowercase).